Architecture plan for myClawTeam static site

Product source
- PRODUCT.md is not present in the initial checkout. Use the issue text as the product source until PRODUCT.md exists.
- Brand/name: myClawTeam.
- Core positioning from Issue #8: "Agent Team for Founders / You just talk, we handle the rest."

Project shape
- Astro static site with Tailwind CSS.
- Keep the page as a mostly static single-page marketing site with small, isolated client-side scripts for mobile nav and preview tabs.
- Produce static output in dist/ for self-hosting; avoid backend services and CI/CD assumptions.

Suggested module structure
- src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro: document shell, metadata, fonts, theme wrapper, skip link, and shared head tags.
- src/pages/index.astro: section composition only; import each section and pass config data.
- src/components/Nav.astro: sticky top navigation and desktop links.
- src/components/MobileNavToggle.astro or inline script in Nav.astro: accessible open/close behavior for small screens.
- src/components/Footer.astro: grouped links, legal/social row, config-driven content.
- src/components/sections/Hero.astro: headline, verbatim product copy, CTAs, dark gradient backdrop.
- src/components/sections/ProductPreview.astro: headline, tabs, framed preview image, tab markup/data attributes.
- src/components/sections/FeatureGrid.astro: six-card feature grid from config or local data.
- src/components/sections/Community.astro: Discord and X/Twitter cards from config.
- src/components/sections/Contact.astro: mailto form that composes subject/body from form fields.
- src/config/site.ts: site metadata, nav anchors, CTA links, social links, mailto target, footer groups, preview tab data, features.
- src/assets/ or public/: logo, preview mockups, and icons. Prefer public/ for directly referenced static images and src/assets/ for imported optimized assets if needed.
- src/styles/global.css: Tailwind layers, CSS variables/design tokens, base element styles, focus states, and smooth scrolling.

Shared types and data
- Define lightweight TypeScript types in src/config/site.ts or src/types/site.ts only if reused across multiple components.
- Suggested types: NavItem, CtaLink, FooterGroup, SocialLink, PreviewTab, FeatureCard.
- Keep all editable URLs and placeholder destinations centralized in site config so later issues do not duplicate links.

Issue dependencies
- Issue #1 creates the Astro skeleton, package scripts, formatting/lint setup, and first build.
- Issue #2 depends on #1 and adds Tailwind plus dark theme tokens.
- Issue #3 depends on #2 and establishes the global layout, base styles, and section anchor scaffolding.
- Issue #4 depends on #1 and adds static assets plus central config.
- Issues #5, #7, #9, #12, and #13 depend on the shared layout/config/assets from #3 and #4.
- Issue #6 depends on #5 because the mobile toggle extends the nav component.
- Issue #8 depends on #3 for section layout and base visual system.
- Issue #10 depends on #9 because it wires behavior into the tabbed preview markup.
- Issue #11 depends on #3 and should use the same card/token patterns as the rest of the page.
- Issues #14 and #15 are cross-cutting QA passes after the main page sections are implemented.
- Issue #16 follows responsive/accessibility work and verifies the built dist output plus links/interactions.
- Issue #17 follows static build verification and documents self-host serving of dist/ with relative asset paths.

Key design decisions
- Use Astro components for page sections and plain TypeScript/JavaScript for the two required interactions. No frontend framework is needed for this scope.
- Keep interaction scripts colocated with the components they enhance, using data attributes instead of brittle selectors.
- Use semantic landmarks and anchors from the first layout implementation so accessibility and smoke testing have stable targets.
- Use Tailwind theme extension plus CSS variables for near-black backgrounds, orange accent tokens, muted text, borders, and focus rings.
- Build assets/config before nav/footer/section work so all links and media are driven from one source.
- For the contact form, submit should update window.location or form action to a composed mailto URL; no backend or third-party service.
- Final deployment prep should document serving dist/ as static files and verify paths work without a dev server.
